INT. NATURAL HISTORY MUSEUM, DINOSAUR HALL - NIGHT

A cathedral of bones. A Diplodocus skeleton arches over the central floor. Moonlight pours through high windows. Somewhere a pipe drips.

A service door clicks open. Six figures in black filter in, silent as cats: CASSIUS OBAYOMI (40s, crew boss, headset), RENATA VOSKUIJLEN (30s, safecracker, tool roll), ILDEFONSO "FONZ" MARBURY (20s, climber, harness), PALOMA TREVINO-HALE (30s, hacker, laptop bag), GUSTAV LINDQVIST (60s, forger, silk gloves), and QUINCY ABERNATHY (20s, driver, nervy).

CASSIUS
(whispering)
Clock's running. Eleven minutes.

Renata crosses to a glass case under the skeleton's ribs, where a fossilized egg sits on velvet. Fonz clips a line to the beam above and begins to ascend. Paloma kneels beside a wall panel, jacks in, and her screen scrolls green code. Gustav circles the display, comparing the egg to a photograph in his palm, while Quincy hovers at the doorway, watching the corridor with his heart in his throat.

PALOMA
Cameras are looped.

CASSIUS
Fonz?

FONZ
(from above)
Almost. Bone's slick.

Renata pries the lock. It pops. She lifts the lid and Gustav, with trembling gloved hands, swaps the real egg for a copy, but a sharp CLICK echoes from the corridor and Quincy swallows, Fonz freezes in mid-swing, Paloma shuts her laptop, and Renata drops flat behind the case.

QUINCY
(hissing)
Guard. Coming this way.

CASSIUS
Positions.

Fonz hauls himself up onto the Diplodocus ribs. Gustav tucks the real egg inside his coat and melts behind a pillar. Paloma and Renata slide under a bench, and Cassius presses against the wall beside the door as a flashlight beam swings across the floor.

A GUARD, a heavyset man in his fifties named ROLAND PIKE, strolls in humming. He pauses at the case. He sweeps his light along the glass. A beat. Another. Cassius raises a fist, ready.

ROLAND
(muttering)
Dang pigeons.

He wanders off. His footsteps fade. The crew exhales as one. Fonz drops silently to the floor and the six of them regroup near the door. Cassius counts heads with a finger.

CASSIUS
Out. Now.

They file through the service door, one by one, Gustav last, cradling the egg like a newborn.

The Diplodocus watches them go.
